---
title: "Scrolling"
description: "Configure scroll gestures and vertical scroll debouncing in AG Grid."
---

By default, the grid uses the browser's native scrolling. Scrollbars appear when rows or columns extend beyond the visible area, and touch or trackpad gestures can scroll both axes at once.

## Scroll Gestures

Register `ScrollGestureModule` and set `scrollGestureMode: 'axisLocked'` to keep touch and trackpad gestures on one axis and reduce accidental diagonal scrolling. The default, `'native'`, leaves scrolling to the browser and does not require the module.

```js
const gridOptions = {
    scrollGestureMode: 'axisLocked',
};
```

Axis-locked touch scrolling uses grid-managed momentum, so its feel differs from native scrolling. Keyboard scrolling and scrollbar dragging are unchanged. Use `api.setGridOption('scrollGestureMode', mode)` to switch modes, as the toggle below demonstrates.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Scroll Gestures" name="scroll-gestures" /%}

## Debounce Vertical Scroll

Set `debounceVerticalScrollbar: true` to delay updating the displayed rows until vertical scrolling pauses. When dragging the vertical scrollbar, the grid waits for a pause before moving to the new position. By default, this option is `false` and the grid follows the scrollbar continuously.

```js
const gridOptions = {
    debounceVerticalScrollbar: true,
};
```

Use the toggle below, then drag the vertical scrollbar to compare the behaviours. This is an initial-only option, so the example recreates the grid when toggled.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Debounce Vertical Scroll" name="debounce-vertical-scroll" /%}
